STM32CubeN6
###########

Origin:
   STMicroelectronics
   https://www.st.com/en/embedded-software/stm32cuben6.html

Status:
   version 1.3.0

Purpose:
   STMicroelectronics official MCU package for STM32N6 series.

Description:
   This package is an extract of official STM32CubeN6 package written by STMicroelectronics.
   It is composed of STM32Cube hardware abstraction layer (HAL) and low layer (LL) plus a set
   of CMSIS headers files, one for each SoC in the STM32N6 series.

Dependencies:
    None.

URL:
   https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeN6

Commit:
   1fc803683e03b0ce78e64523441d31acd0db2829

Maintained-by:
   External

License:
   BSD-3-Clause

License Link:
   https://opensource.org/licenses/BSD-3-Clause

Patch List:
   *Changes from official delivery:
    -dos2unix applied
    -trailing white spaces removed

   *Provision to enable hal & ll asserts added
    -Added stm32cube/stm32n6xx/drivers/include/stm32_assert.h
    -Removed unused stm32cube/stm32n6xx/drivers/include/stm32_assert_template.h

   *Fix to remove PAGESIZE definition which conflicts with POSIX
    Impacted files:
     drivers/include/Legacy/stm32_hal_legacy.h

   *Fix FSBL configuration
    -Turn CMSE_NS_ENTRY modifier, which requires enabling CONFIG_ARM_FIRMWARE_HAS_SECURE_ENTRY_FUNCS
     which we don't need right now, into a no-op.
    Impacted files:
    -soc/system_stm32n6xx_fsbl.c
    -soc/system_stm32n6xx_s.c
    See also:
     https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32/pull/252
     https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32/pull/289

   *Enable all HAL modules
     In the HAL configuration template for STM32N6 series, most modules are
     disabled by default, unlike all other series where they are all enabled.
     Zephyr expects all modules to be enabled since we gate them via CMakeLists
     and Kconfig options instead of preprocessor definitions. Match other series
     by enabling all modules which were not already. Note that the original file
     contains a few duplicate MODULE_ENABLE directives, some of which are enabled
     by default. For the disabled ones, only the first directive is uncommented;
     for the enabled ones, no change is made and the duplicate remains a comment.
    Impacted files:
     stm32n6xx_hal_conf.h
    See also:
     https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32/pull/345

   *Fix XSPIM initialization sequence for XSPI3
     Don't forget to enable XSPI3 clock back when leaving.
    Impacted files:
      stm32cube/stm32n6xx/drivers/src/stm32n6xx_hal_xspi.c
    Internal reference: 212765 (last part)
    See also:
      https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32/pull/340

   *Fix HAL_MDF_IRQHandler
      HAL_MDF_IRQHandler handles IRQ flags in an if {} else if {} condition.
      This causes interrupts to be handled once and only the first flag
      encountered in the condition, while there can be several flags raised.
     Impacted files:
       drivers/src/stm32n6xx_hal_mdf.c
     ST Internal Reference: HAL1-27843

   See release_note.html from STM32Cube
